&lt;p&gt;09&sol;2010 - These individuals who do not have signs or symptoms of tobacco-related disease will be covered under Medicare Part B when the above conditions of coverage are met, subject to certain frequency and other limitations. Effective date 08&sol;25&sol;2010 Implementation date 01&sol;03&sol;2011 (&lt;a href=&quot;https:&sol;&sol;www.cms.gov&sol;Regulations-and-Guidance&sol;Guidance&sol;Transmittals&sol;downloads&sol;R126NCD.pdf&quot;&gt;TN 126&lt;&sol;a&gt;) (CR 7133)&lt;&sol;p&gt;    


&lt;p&gt;    09&sol;2010 - Effective for claims with dates of service on and after August 25, 2010, CMS will cover tobacco cessation counseling for outpatient and hospitalized Medicare beneficiaries:&lt;&sol;p&gt;    
&lt;ol&gt;      
&lt;li&gt;    Who use tobacco, regardless of whether they have signs or symptoms of tobacco-related disease;&lt;&sol;li&gt;  
&lt;li&gt;    Who are competent and alert at the time that counseling is provided; and&lt;&sol;li&gt;  
 &lt;li&gt;    Whose counseling is furnished by a qualified physician or other Medicare-recognized practitioner.&lt;&sol;li&gt;  
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;

indications_limitations:
&lt;p&gt;Cryosurgery of the prostate as a salvage therapy is not covered for any services performed prior to June 30, 2001.&lt;&sol;p&gt;  
  
&lt;p&gt;   Salvage Cryosurgery of Prostate After Radiation Failure. Salvage cryosurgery of the prostate for recurrent cancer is medically necessary and appropriate only for those patients with localized disease who:&lt;&sol;p&gt;  
  
&lt;ol type=&quot;1&quot;&gt;     
&lt;li&gt;   Have failed a trial of radiation therapy as their primary treatment; and&lt;&sol;li&gt;  
  
&lt;li&gt;   Meet one of the following conditions: Stage T2B or below, Gleason score &amp;lt;9, PSA &amp;lt;8 ng&sol;mL.&lt;&sol;li&gt;  
&lt;&sol;ol&gt;  
  
&lt;p&gt;   Cryosurgery as salvage therapy is therefore not covered under Medicare after failure of other therapies as the primary treatment. Cryosurgery as salvage is only covered after the failure of a trial of radiation therapy, under the conditions noted above.&lt;&sol;p&gt;

