&lt;p&gt;06&sol;2013 - Effective for claims with dates of service on and after April 3, 2013, CMS expanded coverage of ocular photodynamic therapy (OPT) with verteporfin for &quot;wet&quot; age-related macular degeneration (AMD) in NCD 80.3.1, Verteporfin.  CMS revised the requirements for testing to permit either optical coherence tomography (OCT) or fluorescein angiography (FA) to assess treatment response.  Corresponding changes are referenced in NCDs 80.3 - Photosensitive Drugs, 80.2 - Photodynamic Therapy, and 80.2.1 - Ocular Photodynamic Therapy (OPT).  Effective date: 04&sol;03&sol;2013 and implementation date: 07&sol;16&sol;2013. (&lt;a href=&quot;https:&sol;&sol;www.cms.gov&sol;Regulations-and-Guidance&sol;Guidance&sol;Transmittals&sol;Downloads&sol;R155NCD.pdf&quot;&gt;TN 155&lt;&sol;a&gt;) (CR 8292)&lt;&sol;p&gt;   

