&lt;p&gt;4. Study Context: The rationale for the study is supported by scientific evidence and study results are expected to fill the specified CMS-identified evidence deficiency and provide evidence sufficient to assess health outcomes.&lt;&sol;p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;5. Study Design: The study design is selected to safely and efficiently generate valid evidence of health outcomes. The sponsors&sol;investigators minimize the impact of confounding and biases on inferences through rigorous design and appropriate statistical techniques. If a contemporaneous comparison group is not included, this choice should be justified, and the sponsors&sol;investigators discuss in detail how the design contributes useful information on issues such as durability or adverse event frequency that are not clearly answered in comparative studies.&lt;&sol;p&gt; 
